{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1085 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "4de1d6b1b5a35a7dd73d706f084924850a37ee1a067b93fa55d2ce83edd27fd8" :edb/db-before-t 1084 :edb/db-after-t 1085 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534397 50 #inst "2026-10-07T00:10:17.908Z" 13194139534397 true] [17592186105842 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286179 13194139534397 true] [17592186105842 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286186 13194139534397 true] [17592186105843 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286193 13194139534397 true] [17592186106134 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534397 true] [17592186106134 1100 "Let $\\mathbf{p} = \\langle  - 1 , 1 , 2 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{q} = \\langle  4 , x , 1 \\rangle  .$. Given that the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q$ is zero, find the value of $x$." 13194139534397 false] [17592186106134 1100 "Let $p=⟨-1,1,2⟩$ and $q=⟨4,x,1⟩.$ Given that the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q$ is zero, find the value of $x.$" 13194139534397 true] [17592186106134 1145 "Since $p$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $q$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\np⊥q\\,⟹\\,p\\cdot q=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y}+{p}_{z}\\cdot {q}_{z} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 4+1\\cdot x+2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =x-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534397 true] [17592186106135 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534397 true] [17592186106135 1100 "Let \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{p} = \\left[ \\begin{array}{c}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n and \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{q} = \\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ 4 \\\\ - 4\\end{array}\\right] .\n$$\n\n. Given that the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q$ is $0$, find the value of $x$." 13194139534397 false] [17592186106135 1100 "Let $p=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $q=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q$ is $0,$ find the value of $x.$" 13194139534397 true] [17592186106135 1145 "Since $p$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $q$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\np⊥q\\,⟹\\,p\\cdot q=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y}+{p}_{z}\\cdot {q}_{z} \\\\  & =6\\cdot x+1\\cdot 4+4\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =6x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ 6x-12 & =0 \\\\ 6x & =12 \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534397 true] [17592186286179 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286180 13194139534397 true] [17592186286179 1089 "q-18372" 13194139534397 true] [17592186286179 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534397 true] [17592186286179 1100 "Let $c=⟨-2,0,0⟩$ and $d=⟨4,-1,0⟩.$ Find the scalar projection of $c$ onto $d.$" 13194139534397 true] [17592186286179 1113 #uuid "a3d78170-5413-5d4e-a05e-ea790601aa25" 13194139534397 true] [17592186286179 1145 "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{d}\\,c & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{|\\,d\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}+{d}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2\\cdot 4+0\\cdot (-1)+0\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{17}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534397 true] [17592186286180 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286181 13194139534397 true] [17592186286180 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286182 13194139534397 true] [17592186286180 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286183 13194139534397 true] [17592186286180 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286184 13194139534397 true] [17592186286180 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286185 13194139534397 true] [17592186286180 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534397 true] [17592186286180 1041 "selection" 13194139534397 true] [175